      "content": "# Bundle patch for dsh-plugin-mac-notify.\n#\n# A profile that lists this package in `dsh.profile.bundles` (which is what\n# `dsh plugin --profile <name> add <spec>` writes) applies this layer and gets\n# the plugin row below. The row names the package itself, so Node resolution\n# finds the installed code from the profile tree.\n#\n# The row deliberately carries no `config`: the plugin's own defaults apply, and\n# a profile that wants different values overrides this row in its own\n# cordis.patch.yml, which is applied after every bundle layer:\n#\n#   - id: mac-notify\n#     name: 'dsh-plugin-mac-notify'\n#     config:\n#       sound: Ping            # 'default' (system alert sound) | a system sound name | 'off'\n#       notifyOnApproval: false\n#       url: 'http://127.0.0.1:3080'\n#\n# Host-only bundle: `apply` subscribes to Host events and shells out to\n# `terminal-notifier` (clickable) or `osascript` (plain banner). There is no\n# browser half, so nothing renders in the page and no page refresh is involved.\n- insert:\n    - id: mac-notify\n      name: 'dsh-plugin-mac-notify'\n"
    }
